  "defect_observations": [
    "C007/C009 proof steps (annex 204-206: limit is F_infinity-measurable because the X_n are; annex 219-221: the event where X_n exceeds E(X_infinity|F_n) by 1/k lies in F_n; annex 234: X_n is F_n-measurable) use adaptedness, which the routed definition def:p15-filtration-martingale (martingales-and-convergence.tex 15-27) defines but does not require. The statements themselves remain true (for a submartingale with an L1 limit, X_infinity <= E(X_infinity|F_infinity) with equal means). The packet's own new convention def:p15-w02c-p15-019-adapted-classes (owned body 36-53) and its relationships paragraph (486-495) state the requirement for exactly these theorems once that file is routed; this is the 162.1 duty for C001 of the martingales-and-convergence unit, not a text gap in this unit.",
    "C012: the stated consequence |Y|<=Z a.s. (body 188) is not given its own line in the proof; it is the pointwise limit of |Y_n|<=Z and is used implicitly in the dominated-convergence step (annex 318-319).",
